# Legacy exports staged for an import.
#
# These are extracts from the live original database — asset values,
# contract references, plot and connection data. They are input to a
# one-off import, not source, and they do not belong in version
# control. Keep them beside the import's SQL on the machine doing the
# load and let them go when it is done.
*/data/*.csv

# Dependencies and build output.
#
# Neither has ever been tracked here, but nothing said so: they were
# kept out by nobody happening to run `git add -A` with a build
# present. That is luck, not a rule, and the first time it ran out the
# commit would carry the whole of node_modules — tens of thousands of
# files and a diff nobody can review.
#
# dist/ has a second reason: a stale copy in the tree can disagree with
# src/, and the one somebody reads to work out what is deployed is the
# wrong one.
node_modules/
dist/
